# Shadow-map resolution A/B in ONE boot ([shadow], 2026-11-16): fast_city3's first still view (the dock: Cole's
# shadow on the planks, the railing and plank stack on the right) for 14 phases of 12 s (8, a 6 s gap, 6 more),
# while tools\shadow_ab.ps1 flips PS3RECOMP_SHADOW_RES, PS3RECOMP_SHADOW_EDGE and PS3RECOMP_SOFT_SHADOWS through
# PS3_TOGGLE_FILE. (A camera pan at 96 s did not turn the camera in run sh2: dropped.) Each phase's shot is taken
# at the end (a shot stalls the game; the window counts the phase minus 1.5 s after the switch). The last shot
# is the menu's Lighting page (the new "Shadow quality" row).
# Run: tools\shadow_ab.ps1 -Tag X -Exe <exe>   (it starts the main tools\fast.ps1 with these steps + the scheduler)
#! seconds 330
#! anchor_range 55:100
#! savefrom work\saves\first-save\gamedata
#! windows 1.5:11.5,13.5:23.5,25.5:35.5,37.5:47.5,49.5:59.5,61.5:71.5,73.5:83.5,85.5:95.5,103.5:113.5,115.5:125.5,127.5:137.5,139.5:149.5,151.5:161.5,163.5:173.5
wait v_02_city_intro 120
sleep 2
# a fixed wait instead of fast_city3's waitimg (the HUD shows ~50 s after the intro): the run goes on, and
# its shots show what was drawn, even when the picture is not the expected one
sleep 52
sleep 2
anchor
at 11.6
shot p0
at 23.6
shot p1
at 35.6
shot p2
at 47.6
shot p3
at 59.6
shot p4
at 71.6
shot p5
at 83.6
shot p6
at 95.6
shot p7
at 113.6
shot p8
at 125.6
shot p9
at 137.6
shot p10
at 149.6
shot p11
at 161.6
shot p12
at 173.6
shot p13
wait \[overlay\] script t=\d+ s: lighting 150
sleep 1.5
shot menu
sleep 0.5
close
